WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.540
Once in a awhile a little voice will pop in
my head and say "Dave, are you sure you aren't

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.690
overblowing any of the big issues you talk
about?

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.580
Maybe the threat to free speech really isn't
so bad!

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.350
Maybe the assault on open discourse on college
campuses isn't all that terrible!

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.500
Maybe most of mainstream media isn't simply
pandering for clicks and views."

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.840
Then, and it NEVER fails, some current event
takes place, reminding me the issues we're

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.629
talking about related to free speech are not
only the most important issues of the day,

00:00:33.629 --> 00:00:37.850
but perhaps we're actually underestimating
the severity of them.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.930
Without an absolute protection of free speech
first, we can't have debates around any of

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.960
the other issues that might be important to
you right now.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.210
Care about Devos' comments on Title 9?

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:54.450
Trumps decision on DACA, or global warming
as it related to the recent spate of hurricanes?

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:59.989
Your freedom of speech and of inquiry is what
guarantees we can have discussions about those

00:00:59.989 --> 00:01:02.010
issues and everything else.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:06.729
Tomorrow, former Rubin Report guest and a
friend of mine Ben Shapiro will be speaking

00:01:06.729 --> 00:01:08.200
at UC Berkeley.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:14.250
The Internet has been lit about the preemptive
protests, counter-protests safe spaces, trigger

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:17.890
warnings for his event, even before the event
has actually happened.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:23.600
Sadly, in and of itself, none of this impending
and hyped up chaos is new, so I wasn't planning

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.049
on addressing it before Ben even had the chance
to speak.

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:31.520
Then I saw a tweet from the Los Angeles Times,
and felt I needed to discuss it with you.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:37.480
The tweet reads, "Berkeley braces for right
wing talk show host Ben Shapiro visit."

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:43.530
Now this headline doesn't seem too bad on
face value, actually it reads very similarly

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.600
to how much of mainstream news is published
these days.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:51.670
If you're looking for it though, and I know
many of you are, the headline is actually

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:55.890
loaded a combination of subtle bias and outright
Fake News.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:02.049
"Berkeley braces" is an interesting choice
of words -- usually in headlines we brace

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:06.110
ourselves for a hurricane, or other natural
disaster.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:11.310
The attempt here, of course, is to compare
Shapiro's words with the same emotional weight

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:14.150
as a natural disaster which can actually end
lives.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:20.299
In a time right after two major storms, Hurricane
Harvey and Hurricane Irma hit the United States,

00:02:20.299 --> 00:02:25.529
this phrasing is particularly useful as we
are all subconsciously are associating the

00:02:25.529 --> 00:02:28.519
word 'brace' with death and destruction.

00:02:28.519 --> 00:02:32.760
If you think I'm overstating the word 'brace'
with hurricanes just do a google news search

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:38.159
for 'braces for Harvey' or 'braces for Irma'
and see what pops up

00:02:38.159 --> 00:02:44.419
Now the Los Angeles Time's reader knows something
so horrible is coming that UC Berkely must

00:02:44.419 --> 00:02:47.480
brace for it as it would for a deadly hurricane.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:54.049
Next, they use the pejorative "right wing"
to opine on Ben's talk show and his views.

00:02:54.049 --> 00:02:59.041
Of course there's no doubt that as a conservative
Ben's political views are on the right, but

00:02:59.041 --> 00:03:02.290
there's something else when they say 'right
wing.'

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:07.049
Virtually every time the mainstream media
uses the phrase 'right wing', it is to paint

00:03:07.049 --> 00:03:11.099
someone as either as scary, evil, or racist.

00:03:11.099 --> 00:03:15.629
In and of itself being 'right wing' isn't
bad, it's just a political view, one which

00:03:15.629 --> 00:03:17.849
you may or may not agree with.

00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:22.359
But here we now have students 'bracing' for
this 'right wing' speaker.

00:03:22.359 --> 00:03:24.029
Sounds scary, doesn't it?

00:03:24.029 --> 00:03:28.650
Why does the mainstream media never label
anyone or anything 'Left Wing' when they want

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:29.650
to scare you?

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:32.969
Has antifa been labeled Left Wing by the LA
Times or CNN?

00:03:32.969 --> 00:03:38.409
I searched LAtimes.com for those words together
and unsurprisingly it has not.

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:43.599
While 'Right Wing' is a dog whistle for bad,
and Left wing is just left out altogether

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:47.510
when it doesn't fit the correct narrative.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:52.829
Did you see a headline in the LA Times or
CNN that read "City Univeristy of New York

00:03:52.829 --> 00:03:57.159
braces for Left Wing Activist Linda Sarsour?"

00:03:57.159 --> 00:04:02.569
Of course you didn't, and I would argue that
her ideas are far more dangerous than anything

00:04:02.569 --> 00:04:04.449
Ben talks about.

00:04:04.449 --> 00:04:08.710
If you think I'm being a bit melodramatic
here, consider this: As long as the LA Times

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:13.949
is using colorful language with their headlines,
why didn't they add a fun adjective before

00:04:13.949 --> 00:04:14.949
UC Berkely.

00:04:14.949 --> 00:04:19.820
I mean Berkely was once the home for free
speech in America and now it is a cesspool

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.530
of left wing...see I can do it too...hate.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:28.939
Why not say "Former School of Academic Freedom
Berkely Braces for Right Wing Talk Show Host

00:04:28.939 --> 00:04:30.449
Ben Shapiro?"

00:04:30.449 --> 00:04:36.010
or "Intolerant of Other Ideas Berkely Braces
for Right Wing Talk Show Host Ben Shapiro?"

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:41.349
Or even simply, and most honestly and directly
if we're being fair to both sides..."Left

00:04:41.349 --> 00:04:46.110
Wing Berkely braces for right wing talk show
host Ben Shapiro."

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:48.370
Certainly that would be true at least.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:54.150
But, their omission of one label while prescribing
another one tells you all you need to know.

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:59.169
This headline, before Ben has even spoken,
tells you a story alright, but it isn't the

00:04:59.169 --> 00:05:01.390
one that the LA Times intended.

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:05.560
The headline tells you the story of the double
standard with which mainstream conservatives

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.259
have to deal with, fueled by a media that
enflames the situation when it comes to anyone

00:05:10.259 --> 00:05:14.840
on the right, but largely ignores it when
it comes to anyone on the Left.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:19.360
This tricky use of words and selective writing
is largely what people are talking about when

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.300
they talk about Fake News.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:26.310
The media should be giving us facts straight
up, not editorializing through headlines that

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:29.639
confused and conflate what's actually happening
on the ground.

00:05:29.639 --> 00:05:34.010
If you'd like to know more on how the media
confuses us with headlines like this, check

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:38.881
out my discussion with Eric Weinstein on The
Russell Conjugation, which we'll link to right

00:05:38.881 --> 00:05:39.960
down below.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:45.190
Ben is going to speak and say some things
that will trigger people, not because they're

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:51.480
attacking individual people or because they're
truly offensive, but more so because he's

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:57.680
challenging the Social Justice Warrior idoeology
that has ransacked clear thinking on the college

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.250
campus in America.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:04.500
If you don't like what he says write a paper
about it, invite a counter speaker, or non-violently

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:10.560
protest in a way which allows the people who
do want to hear him to have their right to

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:14.400
free speech, just as much as you want to have
yours.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:19.370
Headlines like this subtly excuse and actually
help instigate violence towards anyone who

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:21.460
dare step out of group think.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:26.470
I guarantee the ideas that Ben talks about
tomorrow are in no way something you have

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:31.889
to brace for, and even less something you
have to act violently towards.

00:06:31.889 --> 00:06:36.610
Defending free speech as a college student
now will help ensure that it will be defended

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.810
when you grow out of groupthink as an adult.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:44.849
So instead of silencing speakers on campus
perhaps do what you're supposed to in college

00:06:44.849 --> 00:06:49.400
instead: listen to someone who thinks differently
than you do.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:54.379
This way you will learn how to think...and
instead of having to brace yourself for bad

00:06:54.379 --> 00:06:55.290
ideas, you can arm yourself with good ones.

